    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0210" n="44" xml:id="pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 813.00/883a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Fletcher </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-06T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>431. This Government has been asked by Salvador to send representatives to a
                    conference of Central American States to consider renewing Treaty of Washington
                    of 1907.</p>
                <p>Discreetly ascertain and telegraph whether Mexican Government has been asked to
                    be represented at conference, and, if so, what Mexico’s attitude will be.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
